// Row numbers of a buffer (Inputs/index_of.ent): arithmetic with i32s,
// comparisons, casts, `none`, fields of buffers and uniques, fn and proc
// parameters and results, a buffer whose numbers take 16 bits, and a row
// read by one past the rows the buffer has (as it was left, not nought).
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/index_of.ent | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      c 10 back 9 apart 7 w 27
// CHECK-NEXT: marks 9 -1 none true
// CHECK-NEXT: placed 3 w 77 twice 18
// CHECK-NEXT: ~ -10 ^ 8 >> 4 > true == false
// CHECK-NEXT: big 29999 7 0
// CHECK-NEXT: kept 3: by row number 27, by number 0

// As imported, the buffers read by row number have the mark that gives them
// room for a power of two of rows, and the numbers their bits.
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/index_of.ent -I %S/../../devices \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR
// IR-DAG: ent.buffer @Arena (w: i32) capacity 100 {ent.indexed}
// IR-DAG: ent.buffer @Marks (at: !ent.index_of<@Arena, 8>, n: i32) capacity 10
// IR-DAG: ent.buffer @Big (v: i8) capacity 30000 {ent.indexed}
// IR-DAG: ent.buffer.at @Big "v"[%{{.*}} : !ent.index_of<@Big, 16>] : i8
